p.src:
White begins by broadening the word trauma. In his framing, trauma is not only a major injury. It is anything abnormal in day-to-day life experience. He names three main forms: $\text{Trauma}
=
\{\text{toxic},\ \text{physical},\ \text{emotional}\}.$ Toxic trauma includes addiction, alcohol, drugs, food sensitivity, and poisons. Physical trauma includes football injuries, falls, head injuries, traumatic brain injury, and war injuries. Emotional trauma includes loss of a loved one and betrayal by a loved one.

